# =============================================================================
# Client-side configuration — COMMITTED ON PURPOSE
# =============================================================================
# Vite inlines these two values into the browser bundle at BUILD time. Because
# .env is gitignored, it does not exist on Cloudflare’s build machine, so a
# CI build could not read them and shipped a bundle whose Supabase client was
# configured with `undefined` — a site that deploys green and cannot log in.
#
# Committing them is what makes that impossible: the build no longer depends on
# a value someone has to remember to set by hand in a dashboard, and there is
# nothing left for a deploy to wipe.
#
# Safe to commit, and only these two are:
#   - The project URL is already public in wrangler.jsonc.
#   - The anon / publishable key is public by design. It ships to every
#     visitor in the JavaScript bundle already, and row-level security is
#     enabled on all ten tables, so it grants exactly the read policies and
#     nothing more. Every write goes through the Worker.
#
# NEVER add anything else here. A VITE_-prefixed variable is public. The
# service-role key, the JWT secret, the Alpaca and Finnhub keys and the invite
# code are Worker-only — they live in .dev.vars locally and in the Worker
# secret store in production (scripts/push-secrets.ps1).
#
# `npm run build` refuses to run if either value below is missing, templated,
# or is a service-role credential. See scripts/check-client-env.ts.
# =============================================================================

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://vtlqkgpcfdhslqahivzf.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_cuk-R3Ny76fih_Jj52jR_g_9zHctpSH
